  {
   "id": "up-counter",
   "name": "Two-bit up counter",
   "model": "counter",
   "summary": "Counts rising Clock edges from 0 to 3 and wraps. Two copper bulbs hold the bits.",
   "lesson": [
    "A copper bulb flips each time its power rises, so it remembers one bit by itself.",
    "A comparator reads the first bulb and, through a block, keeps a torch off while that bulb is lit.",
    "When the first bulb goes dark the torch relights, a rising edge that flips the second bulb.",
    "That is a carry: the second bulb changes once for every two clock pulses."
   ],
   "controls": {
    "clock": [
     0,
     0,
     0
    ]
   },
   "outputs": {
